<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover_na_extended/legend.png?v=na-cloud-20261013-1540-GDPS-TCC-GDPS_15km_TotalCloudCover-n-5273396-GOES-18-2026-10-13-15-20Z-valid-cells-3435426-GOES-19-2026-10-13-15-20Z-valid-cells-3904271-RRFS-TCDC-rrfs.20261013-n-2632946" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Cloud cover (%, OBSERVED neighborhood fraction from GOES: share of 2 km satellite pixels flagged cloudy around each point): <b>LOWEST 0 clear</b> transparent &rarr; thin cloud <b>dark-blue/blue/cyan</b> &rarr; <b>40 green</b> &rarr; <b>55 yellow</b> &rarr; <b>70 orange</b> &rarr; <b>82 red</b> &rarr; <b>90 magenta</b> &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 100 overcast</b> dark-purple. Same % always shows the same color; clear areas stay see-through. Satellite retrieval where GOES is valid, model fill elsewhere (see provenance).</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT OBSERVATION + MODEL FILL (GOES FD 10-min + RRFS/GDPS fallback)</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA GOES-East (GOES-19) + GOES-West (GOES-18) ABI L2 Clear Sky Mask full-disk observations, RRFS TCDC fallback, GDPS fallback<br/><a href="https://www.goes.noaa.gov/">https://www.goes.noaa.gov/</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p><p><b>Coverage Selector</b> — one coverage at a time (Pro switches exclusively; Web/app: uncheck the others):<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Cloud_Cover_Basin.kml">Great Lakes Basin Coverage</a><br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Cloud_Cover_NorthAmerica.kml">North America Coverage</a><br>◉ <b>Extended North America Coverage</b> (this view)<br>Add once: <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Cloud_Cover_Coverage.kml">Coverage collection file</a> (all three as toggles).</p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE CLOUD COVER — Extended North America Coverage</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p>Cloud cover (%, OBSERVED neighborhood fraction from GOES: share of 2 km satellite pixels flagged cloudy around each point): <b>LOWEST 0 clear</b> transparent &rarr; thin cloud <b>dark-blue/blue/cyan</b> &rarr; <b>40 green</b> &rarr; <b>55 yellow</b> &rarr; <b>70 orange</b> &rarr; <b>82 red</b> &rarr; <b>90 magenta</b> &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 100 overcast</b> dark-purple. Same % always shows the same color; clear areas stay see-through. Satellite retrieval where GOES is valid, model fill elsewhere (see provenance).</p><p><b>Coverage:</b> Extended North America Coverage<br><b>Precedence:</b> 1) Valid GOES-East/GOES-West full-disk BCM (DQF==0). 2) RRFS TCDC where GOES invalid/missing. 3) GDPS TotalCloudCover only for verified remaining gaps. Missing satellite pixels are NEVER rendered as clear sky.<br><b>Provenance:</b> {'GOES-19': '2026-10-13 15:20Z valid-cells=3904271', 'GOES-18': '2026-10-13 15:20Z valid-cells=3435426', 'RRFS-TCDC': 'rrfs.20261013 n=2632946', 'GDPS-TCC': 'GDPS_15km_TotalCloudCover n=5273396'}</p><p><b>Coverage Selector</b> — one coverage at a time (Pro switches exclusively; Web/app: uncheck the others):<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Cloud_Cover_Basin.kml">Great Lakes Basin Coverage</a><br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Cloud_Cover_NorthAmerica.kml">North America Coverage</a><br>◉ <b>Extended North America Coverage</b> (this view)<br>Add once: <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Cloud_Cover_Coverage.kml">Coverage collection file</a> (all three as toggles).</p>]]></description>
      <GroundOverlay>
        <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
        <drawOrder>10</drawOrder>
        <Icon>
          <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover_na_extended/current.png?v=na-cloud-20261013-1540-GDPS-TCC-GDPS_15km_TotalCloudCover-n-5273396-GOES-18-2026-10-13-15-20Z-valid-cells-3435426-GOES-19-2026-10-13-15-20Z-valid-cells-3904271-RRFS-TCDC-rrfs.20261013-n-2632946</href>
          <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
          <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
        </Icon>
        <LatLonBox>
          <north>85.0</north>
          <south>5.0</south>
          <east>-15.0</east>
          <west>-180.0</west>
        </LatLonBox>
      </GroundOverlay>
    </Folder>
